  "limitations": [
    "The test split is previously exposed (PR 38 protocol section 15; contract L1, section 12). Every Stage 4 and crossover result is descriptive; PR 39 claims only what contract section 12 allows.",
    "Abstention, both arbiters: the registered cut maximises F2 on retained training rows subject to coverage >= 0.50 (shared.stage4.tune_min_confidence). F2 has no TN term, so retaining a correct negative never raises it, and abstention can fall mostly on correct negatives: retained precision and recall rise while retained accuracy falls, and retained recall overstates effective recall. The Commit 5 accounting reports this per cell; the protocol is unchanged.",
    "Correction (supersedes the third limitation of the Commit 5 crossover_baseline.json, which is not rewritten). That item attributes the concentration of abstention on negatives in both arbiters to a threshold-relative confidence bound. The bound is structural for the GLASS Arbiter only: a negative vote's confidence is at most its voter's threshold (the Stage 1 and Stage 3 recall cuts, the router's base rate for Pass 1), so a negative decision's weighted confidence cannot exceed the largest of them while a positive decision's can approach one minus the smallest (values: reproduction.json, confidence_room). Meta-XGB's confidence is |p - t| in its raw class-weighted space at one operating threshold t, so its sides have room t and 1 - t (recorded); its abstention pattern needs its own interpretation from its score distribution under the F2 criterion above, and this record makes no claim about its cause.",
    "The coverage floor binds on training rows only; test coverage is reported against it per cell and can fall below it.",
    "The GLASS Arbiter's score is a weighted average of upstream probabilities: it ranks (ROC-AUC, PR-AUC) but is not a calibrated probability, and it is not the arbiter's decision function.",
    "The existing metric code's zero-division conventions (0, and ROC-AUC 0.5 on one class) are reported as undefined by the accounting; no stored value of the accepted arbiters relies on them (A5.4).",
    "The bootstrap resamples test rows with the models fixed; it does not reflect training variability.",
    "Stage 2's role in the final cascade is descriptive (F10); the PR 38 Tier 2 results stay tied to the historical upstream. Stage 4 stacking keeps an indirect upstream dependence (L7, F39).",
    "The pytest 'notebook' marker selects no tests. The notebook evidence is this run's two fresh-kernel, top-to-bottom executions.",
    "The suites emit recurring scikit-learn MLP fixture warnings; their cleanup is PR 40.",
    "Tracked notebook outputs (owner disposition): Retained original repository Venn figure; preserved newly generated figure in the external execution directory. Three tracked MLP CSV files remained unchanged."
  ],
